    "answer": {
      "short": "$107.23\\text{ m}$",
      "worked": "Let $x$ be the horizontal distance from the base of the cliff to the boat. The angle of elevation from the boat is $25^{\\circ}$ because the horizontals are parallel.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\tan(25^{\\circ}) &= \\frac{50}{x}\\\\x &= \\frac{50}{\\tan(25^{\\circ})}\\\\x &\\approx 107.23\\text{ m}\\end{align*}$$",
